{"name":"Old Grey Mare","hex":"#b4b6ad","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"old","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Mochi."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of an object, concept, relationship, etc., having existed for a relatively long period of time.","Of a living being, having lived for most of the expected years."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/old"},{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"},{"term":"mare","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An adult female horse.","A foolish woman."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of evil spirit formerly thought to sit on the chest of a sleeping person; also, the feeling of suffocation felt during sleep, attributed to such a spirit (likely a folkloric interpretation of sleep paralysis).","A nightmare; a frustrating or terrible experience."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mare"}],"entries":[{"title":"The Grey Mare and her Colts","blocks":[{"text":"The Grey Mare and her Colts is a megalithic chambered long barrow located near Abbotsbury in Dorset, England. It was built during the Early and Middle Neolithic periods. The tomb was partially excavated in the early nineteenth century, and was found to contain human bones and several pottery fragments."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/The_Grey_Mare_and_Her_Colts_Long_Barrow._-_geograph.org.uk_-_1123108.jpg/330px-The_Grey_Mare_and_Her_Colts_Long_Barrow._-_geograph.org.uk_-_1123108.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Grey_Mare_and_her_Colts","wikidata":"Q13220450"},{"title":"Mare","blocks":[{"text":"A mare is an adult female horse or other equine. In most cases, a mare is a female horse over the age of three, and a filly is a female horse three and younger. In Thoroughbred horse racing, a mare is defined as a female horse more than four years old. The word can also be used for other female equine animals, particularly mules and zebras, but a female donkey is usually called a \"jenny\". A broodmare is a mare used for breeding."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Lovely_Little_Girl.jpg/330px-Lovely_Little_Girl.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mare","wikidata":"Q1104034"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey","wikidata":"Q42519"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Grey_Mare_and_her_Colts_-_geograph.org.uk_-_180692.jpg/500px-Grey_Mare_and_her_Colts_-_geograph.org.uk_-_180692.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Grey_Mare_and_her_Colts_-_geograph.org.uk_-_180692.jpg/500px-Grey_Mare_and_her_Colts_-_geograph.org.uk_-_180692.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Grey Mare tomb","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGrey_Mare_and_her_Colts_-_geograph.org.uk_-_180692.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Poulain_ardennais_02.jpg/500px-Poulain_ardennais_02.jpg?utm_source=en